# Versioned releases

`main` is the integration trunk. Tags (`vX.Y.Z`) are frozen snapshots. Process: [docs/structured-releases.md](docs/structured-releases.md).

- Land user-visible work on `main` (short feature branches are fine).
- Add a bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) in the same change. Skip for internal refactors, tests, and docs with no user-facing behaviour change.
- Do not bump `cleave.__version__`, add a dated `## [X.Y.Z]` section, tag, or GitHub Release unless asked to cut a release. `__version__` is last-shipped until a cut.
- Do not introduce a long-lived `develop` or `release/*` trunk, GitFlow, or holding features off `main`.

A `release/X.Y` branch is only for a freeze window or a patch of a shipped tag, and only when asked.
